"""Real, independent validation that `gymact.gyms.cloud_topology`'s loaded AWS/Azure/GCP data
was modeled correctly -- not merely that it loaded without raising an exception.

GENERATED by ggen from ggen/cloud-topology-validation-pack/ontology.ttl -- do not hand-edit.
Every provider policy fact (loader/recount function names, staleness threshold, the
degenerate-services exception, the spot-check pair) and every static reason-code string below
is echoed verbatim from that ontology, per pack-authoring-pack's "templates echo, they never
synthesize" rule -- to change the policy, edit the ontology and re-run `ggen sync run`, then
`ggen receipt verify` to get a fresh, durable proof that this file matches it.
`.ggen-v2/receipt.json` is that proof: an actor must not also be the judge of its own outcome
(see gymact/verification.py, combinatorial_ocel.py's `validate_ocel_log`), and neither may this
generated file silently drift from the ontology that is supposed to define it.

Per this repo's own, already-established discipline, every check here either:

1. re-derives a real value from the same raw source data via a SEPARATE code path from
   `cloud_topology.py`'s own loaders (never a second call to the function under test), or
2. checks a real structural invariant against the loaded `CloudTopology` object itself that a
   "did it load" check can never catch (e.g. a service wrongly linked to a region that doesn't
   exist in the same topology).

`cloud_topology.py` itself is NOT generated -- it is imperative I/O against botocore / Azure /
GCP's own public sources, not a projection of admitted ontology facts.
"""

